---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { DIETS } from '../../../data/diets';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Diet Arena: Compare Any Two Diets — Nawtch"
  description="Pick any two popular diets and compare them side by side — typical foods, eating pattern, macro emphasis, evidence strength, and more."
  canonicalPath="/diets/arena/"
  bodyClass="diets"
>
  <header>
    <div class="header-left">
      <h1>Diet Arena</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">Pick any two diets to compare them side by side — same categories, no verdict on which is "better."</p>
    </div>
    <a class="ghost-btn" href="/diets/">← Back to Diets</a>
  </header>

  <div class="settings-section">
    <h2 class="settings-section-title">Choose Two Diets</h2>
    <div class="settings-section-body">
      <div class="add-row add-row-2" style="grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;">
        <div class="field-group">
          <span class="field-label">Diet 1</span>
          <select id="arena-diet-1" onchange="window.arenaSetDiet(1, this.value)">
            <option value="">Select a diet…</option>
            {DIETS.map((d) => <option value={d.slug}>{d.name}</option>)}
          </select>
        </div>
        <div class="field-group">
          <span class="field-label">Diet 2</span>
          <select id="arena-diet-2" onchange="window.arenaSetDiet(2, this.value)">
            <option value="">Select a diet…</option>
            {DIETS.map((d) => <option value={d.slug}>{d.name}</option>)}
          </select>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="field-hint" style="margin-top:14px;font-size:14px;" id="arena-vs-line">Select two diets above to compare them.</p>

      <button class="add-btn" id="arena-compare-btn" style="margin-top:8px;display:none;" onclick="window.arenaGoCompare()">Compare</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="settings-section">
    <h2 class="settings-section-title">About This Comparison Tool</h2>
    <div class="settings-section-body">
      <p class="settings-desc">
        Diet Arena is a side-by-side comparison tool for people who want to understand how two eating patterns
        differ without turning the decision into a single “best diet” verdict. It is built for quick comparisons
        between popular diets, including their typical foods, eating pattern, macro emphasis, and the overall
        strength of evidence behind them.
      </p>
      <p class="settings-desc" style="margin-top: 10px">
        This is useful when you're narrowing down options, exploring a diet for the first time, or trying to
        compare two plans with the same categories in front of you. Instead of reading a long list of pros and cons
        in separate places, you can look at the same structure for both diets and make a more informed comparison.
      </p>
      <p class="settings-desc" style="margin-top: 10px">
        The goal is clarity and context, not a recommendation. Diets vary by goals, food preferences, constraints,
        and evidence quality, and the comparison here is meant to help you understand those differences rather than
        rank one as objectively “better.” See the <a href="/diets/">Diet hub</a> for more diet guides and deeper
        detail on individual approaches.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="info-banners">
    <div class="info-banner">
      <div
        class="info-banner-header"
        onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')"
      >
        <div
          class="info-dot"
          style="
            background: var(--accent);
            box-shadow: 0 0 6px var(--accent);
          "
        ></div>
        <h2 class="info-banner-label">How Diet Arena Works</h2>
        <span class="info-banner-chevron">▼</span>
      </div>
      <div class="info-banner-body">
        Pick any two diets from the dropdowns and then tap <strong>Compare</strong>. The page lines up the same
        categories for both diets so you can quickly see how their eating patterns, food emphasis, and overall
        dietary structure differ side by side.
        <br /><br />
        The comparison is designed to be straightforward and consistent: each diet is reviewed through the same lens,
        which makes it easier to compare options without bouncing between separate pages. Everything here is meant
        to help you understand the trade-offs, not to replace a clinician or personalized nutrition plan.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="info-banner">
      <div
        class="info-banner-header"
        onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')"
      >
        <div
          class="info-dot"
          style="
            background: var(--accent3);
            box-shadow: 0 0 6px var(--accent3);
          "
        ></div>
        <h2 class="info-banner-label">What This Comparison Does and Doesn't Do</h2>
        <span class="info-banner-chevron">▼</span>
      </div>
      <div class="info-banner-body">
        This tool is a <strong>reference and comparison tool</strong>. It helps you understand the broad structure of
        a diet, the kinds of foods it tends to include, and how evidence strength and dietary priorities may differ
        across approaches.
        <br /><br />
        It is not a personalized medical recommendation, a verdict on which diet is “best,” or a substitute for
        individualized advice from a doctor, dietitian, or qualified clinician. The right choice depends on your
        goals, nutrition needs, preferences, health conditions, and how realistic the pattern is for your daily life.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <script type="application/json" id="arena-diets-data" is:inline set:html={JSON.stringify(DIETS.map((d) => ({ slug: d.slug, name: d.name })))} />
  <script src="../../../islands/vanilla/diet-arena/picker.js"></script>
</BaseLayout>
